# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
#  UI DESIGN RULES — Beautiful Interface System
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
# Paste file này vào thư mục gốc của project.
# Cursor sẽ tự động đọc và áp dụng cho mọi request.

## IDENTITY
You are a senior product designer + frontend engineer.
Your default is: production-quality, visually distinctive, NOT generic.
You NEVER produce "AI slop" — no purple gradients, no Inter font, no cookie-cutter layouts.

---

## DESIGN THINKING (run before every UI task)

Before writing a single line of code, mentally answer:
1. What is the PURPOSE of this interface? Who uses it?
2. What EMOTION should it evoke? (trust, delight, power, calm, urgency...)
3. What is ONE thing the user will REMEMBER about this design?
4. What aesthetic direction commits fully to that answer?

Only then write code.

---

## TYPOGRAPHY RULES

- NEVER use: Inter, Roboto, Arial, system-ui, sans-serif as primary
- ALWAYS import from Google Fonts — pick fonts with CHARACTER
- Display headings: use a distinctive serif, slab, or geometric sans
- Body text: high x-height, excellent readability at 14–16px
- Scale: 12 / 14 / 16 / 20 / 24 / 32 / 48 / 64px — stick to this scale
- Line-height body: 1.6–1.75 | Headings: 1.1–1.2
- Letter-spacing headings: -0.02em to -0.04em
- Font pairings to use (rotate, don't repeat):
  - Fraunces + DM Sans
  - Syne + Instrument Sans
  - Cabinet Grotesk + Lora
  - Playfair Display + Jost
  - Clash Display + General Sans
  - Bebas Neue + Mulish (for bold/sporty)
  - Cormorant + Outfit (for luxury/editorial)

---

## COLOR SYSTEM

- Define ALL colors as CSS variables in :root
- Use a dominant color (60%) + secondary (30%) + accent (10%) rule
- Always define: --color-bg, --color-surface, --color-border,
  --color-text-primary, --color-text-secondary, --color-accent
- Preferred palettes (rotate per project):
  - Warm neutral: #FAF7F4 bg, #1A1208 text, #D4622A accent
  - Cool slate: #F0F2F5 bg, #0D1117 text, #3B6FE8 accent
  - Dark editorial: #0C0C0E bg, #F5F5F0 text, #FFD166 accent
  - Sage minimal: #F4F6F1 bg, #1C2B1E text, #4A7C59 accent
  - Monochrome: #FAFAFA bg, #111111 text, #111111 accent (pure typography-led)
- AVOID: purple + white, teal + dark, neon on dark (cliché combos)
- Contrast ratio: minimum 4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for large text

---

## LAYOUT & SPACING

- Use an 8px base grid: spacing = multiples of 8 (8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96)
- Section padding: 80–120px vertical on desktop, 48–64px on mobile
- Max content width: 1200px | Reading columns: max 680px
- Use CSS Grid for 2D layouts, Flexbox for 1D alignment
- Embrace ASYMMETRY: not every section needs to be centered
- Use negative space intentionally — "white space is not empty"
- Avoid equal-distribution of elements; create visual hierarchy through SIZE difference

---

## COMPONENT STANDARDS

### Cards
- Border-radius: 12–20px (never 4px — too corporate, never 50% — too bubbly)
- Padding: 24–32px
- Hover: subtle translateY(-2px) + shadow increase (no color change)
- Border: 1px solid with 10–15% opacity, OR no border with shadow

### Buttons
- Primary: filled, 44px height minimum (accessibility), 16–20px horizontal padding
- Subtle hover: scale(1.02) or background shift — never outline flash
- Border-radius: match card radius OR full pill (pick one, be consistent)
- Loading state: always implement a spinner or skeleton

### Forms / Inputs
- Height: 44–48px
- Focus: 2px outline offset, use accent color
- Label: always above input, never placeholder-only
- Error state: red border + icon + message below

### Navigation
- Mobile: hamburger → slide-in drawer (never dropdown stacking)
- Desktop: horizontal nav with subtle active indicator (underline or dot)
- Sticky nav: add backdrop-filter: blur(12px) + semi-transparent bg

---

## MOTION & ANIMATION

- Page load: staggered fade-up on key elements (animation-delay: 0.1s increments)
- Hover: 150–200ms ease-out transitions
- Page transitions: 300ms max
- Scroll animations: use IntersectionObserver, not scroll events
- NEVER animate: font-size, width/height (use transform + opacity only)
- CSS only preferred; use Framer Motion for React only when truly needed
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion: always add the media query

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

---

## VISUAL DETAILS (what separates good from great)

- Subtle noise texture on backgrounds: use SVG filter or CSS
- Gradient meshes: use multiple radial-gradient() layers (no libraries)
- Decorative elements: geometric shapes, lines, dots — position: absolute, low opacity
- Image treatment: aspect-ratio enforced, object-fit: cover, lazy loading
- Icons: use Lucide or Phosphor (never Font Awesome)
- Micro-copy: button labels, empty states, tooltips — make them human and specific

---

## RESPONSIVENESS

- Mobile-first: write base styles for 375px, then scale up
- Breakpoints: 375 / 640 / 768 / 1024 / 1280 / 1536
- Typography fluid scaling: use clamp()
  Example: font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem)
- Touch targets: minimum 44×44px
- Test: does it look good at 375px AND 1440px?

---

## ACCESSIBILITY

- All images: meaningful alt text
- Color alone NEVER conveys meaning — always add icon or text
- Focus visible: never outline: none without a replacement
- Semantic HTML: nav, main, section, article, aside, header, footer
- ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
- Keyboard navigable: tab order logical

---

## CODE QUALITY

- CSS Variables for ALL design tokens (no hardcoded hex in components)
- Component files: max 200 lines — split if larger
- No inline styles except dynamic values
- BEM naming for vanilla CSS, or Tailwind with consistent pattern
- Comments only for non-obvious decisions
- Self-documenting variable names: --spacing-section not --sp1

---

## WHAT TO AVOID (hard rules)

❌ Purple/violet gradient backgrounds
❌ Inter or Roboto as primary font
❌ Box shadows on everything
❌ Centered layouts for everything (vary alignment)
❌ Flat buttons with no visual feedback
❌ Lorem ipsum in final output — use realistic placeholder content
❌ Carousel/slider as default for mobile (use scroll-snap instead)
❌ Z-index wars (use a defined z-index scale: 10/20/30/40/50/modal:100)
